WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.940
But when they did leave [the coast], where did they go?

2
00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:05.620
When they leave from Bay St. Elaine and they come to Cocodrie.

3
00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:10.100
Like the people from Cocodrie was used to leave and go to Chauvin.

4
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.720
Then through the years with the hurricanes, people started moving further up.

5
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:19.060
Now if we would have had the regulations that we got today—if you want to build,

6
00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:25.807
you got to elevate your camp up—if they'd have done that forty, fifty years ago, we'd still have a lot of people living at Cocodrie.

7
00:00:25.807 --> 00:00:31.020
So the answer to that is, elevate your camp, the hurricane comes, water goes underneath.

8
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:35.540
In those days, people had . . . It was all small camps and they're all almost on the ground,

9
00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.380
just two, three feet high they put them.

10
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:43.280
Well, when the hurricane would come . . . well not exactly every time, it would wash away.

11
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:48.560
What they would do, every one of them rooms, they would cut a hole in the floor two feet by two feet.

12
00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:54.520
When the hurricanes come, you just pull that plug out and the water comes in and the water goes back out.

13
00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:58.360
There was no insulation or nothing like in today's world, you know.

14
00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:00.920
And that's how they survived through all of that.

15
00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:05.680
But we would get a hurricane in Cocodrie and you could come the day after the hurricane . . . you could come to Cocodrie,

16
00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:06.700
there's no more water.

17
00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:10.180
You got a mess, you got mud in your yard, but there's no more water.

18
00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:14.740
Well, when you get to Chauvin, Houma, stuff like that, it's all along the levee.

19
00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.800
Once the levee breaks over, you got a bathtub.

20
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:19.720
It takes three or four weeks before it dries out.

21
00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:25.967
So they're in worse shape being inside the levee than if you was outside the levee.
